@startuml
!include ../rixte/shortfall/style.iuml
title Invalid generate-plan arguments: preserve the cause and recover
autonumber
actor User
participant "<u>MishMash</u>" as App
participant "parser: Parser" as Parser
participant "planParser: GeneratePlanParser" as PlanParser
participant "logger: Logger" as Logger

User -> App : generate-plan d/0
activate App
App -> App : executeCommand(input, scanner, book)
activate App
App -> Parser : parseCommand(input)
activate Parser
note right of Parser : Named-command dispatch is condensed.
Parser -> Parser : parseGeneratePlan("d/0")
activate Parser
create PlanParser
Parser -> PlanParser : new GeneratePlanParser()
Parser -> PlanParser : parse("d/0")
activate PlanParser
PlanParser -> PlanParser : splitIntoValues(args)
activate PlanParser
PlanParser --> PlanParser : values containing d/0
deactivate PlanParser
PlanParser -> PlanParser : parseDays("0")
activate PlanParser
create participant "cause: IllegalArgumentException" as Cause
PlanParser -> Cause : new IllegalArgumentException(error)
PlanParser --> Parser : throws cause
deactivate PlanParser
deactivate PlanParser
note right of Parser
  Catch IllegalArgumentException.
  Append GENERATE_PLAN_USAGE if not already present.
end note
create participant "error: MishMashException" as Error
Parser -> Error : new MishMashException(message, cause)
Parser --> Parser : propagates error
deactivate Parser
Parser --> App : throws error
deactivate Parser
App -> Logger : log(FINE, "Command rejected", error)
App -> App : displayError(error)
note right of App : Print "Error: " + message, including generate-plan usage.\nThe cause is retained for logs, not printed as a console stack trace.
App --> App : executeCommand returns
deactivate App
App -> App : displayCommandPrompt()
App --> User : divider and next-command prompt
deactivate App

note over App, Error
  No GeneratePlanCommand is constructed or executed; recipes, plan, targets, and groceries remain unchanged.
  This sequence depicts the parser cause-preservation contribution, not ownership of the original command.
  Static helpers splitIntoValues and parseDays are shown on the planParser lifeline to keep the view compact.
  Valid requests can reach the existing generator, whose added assertions check day count and recipe prerequisites.
  Its FINE diagnostics report request sizes, target presence, and matching-candidate counts; those paths are not run here.
  GeneratePlanCommand also wraps generation failures with their cause. Related list/delete validation uses the same pattern.
end note
@enduml
